0103-venus-gpu-inject -- DRAFT, not built, not booted, not verified on the device.

Process injection for backboardd (it loads the GPU's OpenGL ES library through
DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES), ported from Topaz's xnu patches onto our Venus chain.

  - bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c: the built-in policy is named "AMFI" and answers dyld's
    __mac_syscall query (call 0x5a) by allowing the DYLD_* variables. From Topaz
    0902 (topaz-0109, AMFI dyld policy answer), together with the policy rename
    and the mpo_policy_syscall hook of Topaz 0147 it depends on. The
    SweetFramebuffer.cpp RedwoodWaitsForGPU hunk of 0902 is left out (not in this
    patch's files, see notes.md).
  - bsd/kern/kern_exec.c: logs whether backboardd starts with DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES
    (Topaz 0914); kern.exec_inject sysctl plus a DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES entry for
    the named programs and for "*app" (every program in an .app bundle), boot-arg
    sweetinject with topaz_inject still accepted (Topaz 0919, 0947); applog and
    applog_name, os_log to the console (Topaz 0920, 0921).
  - bsd/kern/kern_memorystatus.c: no jetsam memory limit for backboardd (Topaz 0915).

Sources: Topaz's xnu patches in refs/ios-topaz/xnu/patches (0902, 0914, 0915, 0919,
0920, 0921, 0947), which derive from HackiOS (OOSEX GANG, APSL 2.0,
https://github.com/oosexgang/hackios-xnu-kernel). Credit to Topaz and HackiOS.
License: Apple Public Source License 2.0, like XNU (see CREDITS.md in refs/ios-topaz).

diff --git a/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c b/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
--- a/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
@@ -374,8 +374,47 @@ sweet_sandbox_syscall(struct proc *p, int call, user_addr_t arg)
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * topaz: dyld asks the policy named "AMFI" (__mac_syscall) what it may do for
+ * the process it starts. Without an answer it runs restricted and ignores the
+ * DYLD_* variables; allowing them lets a library of ours into backboardd
+ * (DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES in its launchd job: the GPU's OpenGL ES library).
+ * Argument: { u64 flags in, user pointer to u64 flags out }.
+ *
+ * Everything else libamfi asks (amfi_interface_query_bootarg_state() in
+ * ExtensionFoundation, ...) succeeds and leaves the caller's output alone:
+ * ENOSYS made lsd's ExtensionKit say "Unable to find AMFI".
+ */
+#define SWEET_AMFI_CHECK_DYLD_POLICY    0x5a
+#define SWEET_AMFI_DYLD_ALLOW_ALL       0xffULL
+
+static int
+sweet_amfi_syscall(__unused struct proc *p, int call, user_addr_t arg)
+{
+	uint64_t in_out[2] = { 0, 0 };
+	uint64_t allow = SWEET_AMFI_DYLD_ALLOW_ALL;
+	int error;
+
+	if (call != SWEET_AMFI_CHECK_DYLD_POLICY) {
+		static uint64_t seen;
+		if (call >= 0 && call < 64 && !(seen & (1ULL << call))) {
+			seen |= 1ULL << call;
+			char name[32];
+			proc_selfname(name, sizeof(name));
+			printf("SWEET AMFI: syscall %d from %s\n", call, name);
+		}
+		return 0;
+	}
+	error = copyin(arg, in_out, sizeof(in_out));
+	if (error == 0) {
+		error = copyout(&allow, (user_addr_t)in_out[1], sizeof(allow));
+	}
+	return error;
+}
+
 static const struct mac_policy_ops sweet_amfi_mac_ops = {
 	.mpo_vnode_check_signature = sweet_amfi_vnode_check_signature,
+	.mpo_policy_syscall = sweet_amfi_syscall,
 };
 
